- [ ] **Step 2: Extract per-request latency from the pcap**

Same technique as `snmpwalk/RESULT-task3.txt`'s METHOD section: match request/response
by `snmp.request_id`.

```bash
cd ~/pcap
PCAP=$(ls -t phase2-mxportdb-*.pcapng | head -1)
tshark -r "$PCAP" -T fields -e frame.time_epoch -e snmp.data -e snmp.request_id 2>/dev/null | awk -F'\t' '
$3!="" {
  if ($2=="0") { t[$3]=$1 }
  else if ($2=="2" && ($3 in t)) { printf "%.3f\n", ($1-t[$3])*1000; delete t[$3] }
}' | sort -n | awk '{v[NR]=$1} END{printf "n=%d p50=%.1fms p95=%.1fms p100=%.1fms\n", NR, v[int(NR*0.5)], v[int(NR*0.95)], v[NR]}'
```

